-- title:
--   Algebra-valued character on a multiplicative spanning family
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $F$ and $L$ be commutative $K$-algebras, let $\iota$ be an index type and let $t : \iota \to F$ and $a : \iota \to L$ be families. Assume: (i) there is an index $i_0$ with $t_{i_0} = 1$ and $a_{i_0} = 1$; (ii) for all $i, j$ there is an index $k$ with $t_k = t_i t_j$ and $a_k = a_i a_j$, so that the family $(t_i)$ is closed under multiplication and the prescribed values multiply accordingly; and (iii) every finite $K$-linear relation among the $t_i$ is also satisfied by the corresponding $a_i$, that is, for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$, every $\mathrm{idx} : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \iota$ and every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to K$, the vanishing of $\sum_l c_l \cdot t_{\mathrm{idx}(l)}$ in $F$ forces the vanishing of $\sum_l c_l \cdot a_{\mathrm{idx}(l)}$ in $L$. Then there exists a $K$-algebra homomorphism $\chi$ from the $K$-subalgebra $\mathrm{adjoin}_K(\mathrm{range}\,t)$ of $F$ generated by the $t_i$ to $L$ such that $\chi(t_i) = a_i$ for every $i$, where $t_i$ is viewed in the subalgebra via the inclusion of the generating set.
--
--   This is the standard construction of a character on a subalgebra generated by a multiplicatively closed spanning family from the consistency of its linear relations, here with values in an arbitrary commutative $K$-algebra rather than in $K$ itself. It is used in the construction of algebra homomorphisms out of the field of modular functions of full level, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algHom_modularFunctionFieldFullC_of_ringHom_admissible`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algHom_modularFunctionFieldFullC_of_ringHom_admissible) and its variant for prime level.
